# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# denylist.txt — customer/partner-specific forbidden terms (git-ignored).
#
# COPY this file to  _private/denylist.txt  and fill in the REAL terms you
# never want to appear in a public commit. One extended-regex pattern per line.
# Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# The whole _private/ folder is git-ignored, so the real terms are never
# published. scripts/check-sensitive.sh reads _private/denylist.txt at commit
# time and blocks any staged change that contains a match.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Customer name (Latin + native script), e.g.:
# Contoso[[:space:]]*Corp
# חברת[[:space:]]*דוגמה

# Partner / author names:
# Firstname[[:space:]]*Lastname

# Real subscription short-codes used in resource names (the numeric IDs).
# Replace the fake examples below with your real codes in _private/denylist.txt:
# \b00001\b
# \b00002\b
# \b00003\b

# Org / naming prefix embedded in resource names:
# azr-[a-z]+-<realprefix>-

# Any other project-specific identifiers:
